@lang en

-- us-ch3-codes.l4 : Title 1, chapter 3, sections 201 to 208 and 210 to 213, and the rest of section 202 (the Code of Laws of the
-- United States and the District of Columbia Code, and their supplements). Section 204 is in us-evidence-of-law.l4, and
-- section 209 too, because both say what is evidence of what.
-- Source: usc01.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text); quotation lines copy it.
--
-- A "shall be dispensed with" or "may be directed" here is a power or duty of a committee or an officer. Each function says what
-- the section provides on the facts given, as a number or a BOOLEAN, and does not predict that the committee will act.
-- Numbers of copies are computed where the text gives a rule for them. Where the text names only an authority or a duty to print
-- "in such form and style ... as may be prescribed" the section is INERT, with the reason beside it.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `us-nouns`
IMPORT `us-interpretation-time`

§ `Chapter 3 - Code of Laws of United States and Supplements; District of Columbia Code and Supplements`

§§ `Section 201 - Publication and distribution`

-- INERT, the lead-in of section 201: "In order to avoid duplication and waste". A statement of purpose that no limb reads.
-- src:213 | Publication in slip or pamphlet form or in the Statutes at Large of any of the volumes or publications enumerated in sections 202 and 203 of this title, shall, in event of enactment, be dispensed with whenever the Committee on the Judiciary of the House of Representatives so directs the Archivist of the United States;
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 201(a) (src:213)
GIVEN `the volume or publication is one enumerated in section 202 or section 203` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the volume or publication has been enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Committee on the Judiciary of the House of Representatives so directs the Archivist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 201(a) dispenses with publication in slip or pamphlet form or in the Statutes at Large` `the volume or publication is one enumerated in section 202 or section 203` `the volume or publication has been enacted` `the Committee on the Judiciary of the House of Representatives so directs the Archivist` MEANS
        `the volume or publication is one enumerated in section 202 or section 203`
    AND `the volume or publication has been enacted`
    AND `the Committee on the Judiciary of the House of Representatives so directs the Archivist`

-- "may be directed by such committee, except that the Director ... shall print such numbers as are necessary for depository
-- library distribution and for sale": the curtailment cannot take the number below what those two purposes need (fork F-201b;
-- the other reading adds the two numbers).
-- src:215 | Curtailment of the number provided by law to be printed and distributed of the volumes or publications enumerated in sections 202 and 203 of this title may be directed by such committee, except that the Director of the Government Publishing Office shall print such numbers as are necessary for depository library distribution and for sale; and
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 201(b) (src:215)
GIVEN `the volume or publication is one enumerated in section 202 or section 203` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number the Committee directs to be printed and distributed` IS A NUMBER
      `the number necessary for depository library distribution and for sale` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number to be printed and distributed once section 201(b) is applied` MEANS
    IF `the volume or publication is one enumerated in section 202 or section 203`
    THEN max `the number the Committee directs to be printed and distributed` `the number necessary for depository library distribution and for sale`
    ELSE `section 201(b) speaks only to the volumes and publications enumerated in sections 202 and 203`

-- src:215 | Curtailment of the number provided by law to be printed and distributed of the volumes or publications enumerated in sections 202 and 203 of this title may be directed by such committee, except that the Director of the Government Publishing Office shall print such numbers as are necessary for depository library distribution and for sale; and
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 201(b) (src:215): the section names only the volumes and publications enumerated in sections 202 and 203
GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 201(b) speaks only to the volumes and publications enumerated in sections 202 and 203` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 201(b) speaks only to the volumes and publications enumerated in sections 202 and 203"

-- src:217 | Such committee may direct that the printing and distribution of any supplement to the Code of Laws of the United States or to the Code of the District of Columbia be dispensed with entirely, except that there shall be printed and distributed for each Congress at least one supplement to each such code, containing the legislation of such Congress.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 201(c) (src:217)
GIVEN `the number of other supplements to the code, containing the legislation of the Congress, to be printed and distributed for the Congress` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 201(c) lets the Committee dispense with the printing and distribution of the supplement` `the number of other supplements to the code, containing the legislation of the Congress, to be printed and distributed for the Congress` MEANS
    `the number of other supplements to the code, containing the legislation of the Congress, to be printed and distributed for the Congress` AT LEAST 1

§§ `Section 202 - Preparation and publication of Codes and Supplements`

-- INERT, section 202(a) and (b): a supplement for each session of the Congress to the then current edition of each code, "cumulatively
-- embracing the legislation of the then current supplement, and correcting errors". A duty of preparation owed to a committee, with no test
-- on facts that a program reads.
-- INERT, section 202(c), the sentence "Copies of each such edition shall be distributed in the same manner as provided in the case of
-- supplements to the code of which it is a new edition": a pointer to the manner of distribution, which section 202 does not state.
-- src:227 | In the case of each code new editions shall not be published oftener than once in each five years. Copies of each such edition shall be distributed in the same manner as provided in the case of supplements to the code of which it is a new edition. Supplements published after any new edition shall not contain the legislation of supplements published before such new edition.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 202(c) (src:227)
GIVEN `the day the previous new edition was published` IS A DATE
      `the day the new edition would be published` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 202(c) allows a new edition to be published on the day` `the day the previous new edition was published` `the day the new edition would be published` MEANS
    `the day the new edition would be published` AT LEAST (`the day that is a number of years after a date` 5 `the day the previous new edition was published`)

-- src:227 | Supplements published after any new edition shall not contain the legislation of supplements published before such new edition.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 202(c) (src:227)
GIVEN `the supplement was published after a new edition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contains the legislation of a supplement published before that new edition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 202(c) forbids the supplement to contain the legislation of an earlier supplement` `the supplement was published after a new edition` `it contains the legislation of a supplement published before that new edition` MEANS
        `the supplement was published after a new edition`
    AND `it contains the legislation of a supplement published before that new edition`

§§ `Section 203 and sections 205 and 206`

-- INERT, section 203: "The Committee on the Judiciary ... is authorized to print bills to codify, revise, and reenact the general and
-- permanent laws relating to the District of Columbia". A bare authorisation, with no condition.
-- INERT, section 205: the publications "shall be printed at the Government Publishing Office and shall be in such form and style and with
-- such ancillaries as may be prescribed by the Committee"; the Librarian "is directed to cooperate"; thumb insets, slips, paper and binding
-- "as may be prescribed". The content is left to the committee, which is not asked in this text.
-- INERT, section 206: bills and resolutions on revision "shall be printed in such form and style, and with such ancillaries, as such committee
-- may prescribe as being economical and suitable", and the committee "may also curtail the number of copies". Same reason as section 205.

§§ `Section 207 - Slip copies of Acts and resolutions`

-- "twenty copies in slip form of each public Act and joint resolution": "public" is read to qualify "Act" only, so a joint resolution of any
-- kind is covered (fork F-207). A private Act is not named, and the answer for it is NOTHING: section 207 directs none.
-- src:257 | The Director of the Government Publishing Office is directed to print, in addition to the number provided by existing law, and, as soon as printed, to distribute in such manner as the Committee on the Judiciary of the House of Representatives shall determine, twenty copies in slip form of each public Act and joint resolution.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 207 (src:257)
GIVEN `it is a public Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a joint resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the number of additional copies in slip form that section 207 directs to be printed` `it is a public Act` `it is a joint resolution` MEANS
    IF `it is a public Act` OR `it is a joint resolution`
    THEN JUST 20
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 208 - Delegation of function to other agencies`

-- src:261 | The functions vested by sections 201, 202, 204–207 of this title in the Committee on the Judiciary of the House of Representatives may from time to time be vested in such other agency as the Congress may by concurrent resolution provide: Provided, That the printing, binding, and distribution of the volumes and publications enumerated in sections 202, 203 of this title shall be done under the direction of the Joint Committee on Printing.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 208, first limb (src:261)
GIVEN `the number of the section that vests the function` IS A NUMBER
      `Congress so provides by concurrent resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 208 allows the function to be vested in another agency` `the number of the section that vests the function` `Congress so provides by concurrent resolution` MEANS
        (   `the number of the section that vests the function` EQUALS 201
         OR `the number of the section that vests the function` EQUALS 202
         OR (   `the number of the section that vests the function` AT LEAST 204
             AND `the number of the section that vests the function` AT MOST 207))
    AND `Congress so provides by concurrent resolution`

-- src:261 | Provided, That the printing, binding, and distribution of the volumes and publications enumerated in sections 202, 203 of this title shall be done under the direction of the Joint Committee on Printing.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 208, the proviso (src:261)
GIVEN `the volume or publication is one enumerated in section 202 or section 203` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 208 puts the printing, binding and distribution under the direction of the Joint Committee on Printing` `the volume or publication is one enumerated in section 202 or section 203` MEANS
    `the volume or publication is one enumerated in section 202 or section 203`

§§ `Section 210 - Distribution of Supplements; slip and pamphlet copies`

-- INERT, section 210 first limb: copies "shall be distributed by the Superintendent of Documents in the same manner as bound volumes of
-- the Statutes at Large". The manner of distribution of those volumes is not stated in Title 1.
-- src:269 | no slip or pamphlet copies of the Code of Laws relating to the District of Columbia, and of the supplements provided for by sections 202, 203 of this title need be printed or distributed.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 210, the proviso (src:269)
GIVEN `it is a slip or pamphlet copy of the Code of Laws relating to the District of Columbia or of a supplement provided for by section 202 or section 203` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 210 says the copy need not be printed or distributed` `it is a slip or pamphlet copy of the Code of Laws relating to the District of Columbia or of a supplement provided for by section 202 or section 203` MEANS
    `it is a slip or pamphlet copy of the Code of Laws relating to the District of Columbia or of a supplement provided for by section 202 or section 203`

§§ `Section 211 - Copies to Members of Congress`

-- Ten copies of each of the District of Columbia Code with tables, index and other ancillaries and of the supplements to both codes for
-- each Member of the Senate and House of Representatives of the Congress in which the original authorized publication is made; for the
-- Judiciary Committees of both Houses "a number of bound copies of each equal to ten times the number of members of such committees";
-- and "one bound copy of each for the use of each committee of the Senate and House of Representatives".
-- src:273 | In addition to quotas provided for by section 210 of this title there shall be printed, published, and distributed of the Code of Laws relating to the District of Columbia with tables, index, and other ancillaries, suitably bound and with thumb inserts and other convenient devices to distinguish the parts, and of the supplements to both codes as provided for by sections 202, 203 of this title, ten copies of each for each Member of the Senate and House of Representatives of the Congress in which the original authorized publication is made, for his use and distribution, and in addition for the Committee on the Judiciary of the House of Representatives and the Committee on the Judiciary of the Senate a number of bound copies of each equal to ten times the number of members of such committees, and one bound copy of each for the use of each committee of the Senate and House of Representatives.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 211 (src:273)
GIVEN `the number of Members of the Senate and House of Representatives of the Congress` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members of the two Committees on the Judiciary` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of committees of the Senate and House of Representatives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of copies of each publication that section 211 requires, in addition to the quotas of section 210` MEANS
        10 TIMES `the number of Members of the Senate and House of Representatives of the Congress`
      + 10 TIMES `the number of members of the two Committees on the Judiciary`
      + `the number of committees of the Senate and House of Representatives`

§§ `Section 212 - Additional distribution at each new Congress`

-- src:277 | In addition the Superintendent of Documents shall, at the beginning of the first session of each Congress, supply to each Senator and Representative in such Congress, who may in writing apply for the same, one copy each of the Code of Laws of the United States, the Code of Laws relating to the District of Columbia, and the latest supplement to each code: Provided, That such applicant shall certify in his written application for the same that the volume or volumes for which he applies is intended for his personal use exclusively: And provided further, That no Senator or Representative during his term of service shall receive under this section more than one copy each of the volumes enumerated herein.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 212 (src:277)
GIVEN `the person is a Senator or Representative in the Congress` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the beginning of the first session of the Congress` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has applied in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has certified in the application that the volume is intended for personal use exclusively` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the volume is the Code of Laws of the United States, the Code of Laws relating to the District of Columbia, or the latest supplement to either` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of copies of that volume the person has already received under section 212 during the term of service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 212 requires the Superintendent of Documents to supply the person one copy of the volume` `the person is a Senator or Representative in the Congress` `it is the beginning of the first session of the Congress` `the person has applied in writing` `the person has certified in the application that the volume is intended for personal use exclusively` `the volume is the Code of Laws of the United States, the Code of Laws relating to the District of Columbia, or the latest supplement to either` `the number of copies of that volume the person has already received under section 212 during the term of service` MEANS
        `the person is a Senator or Representative in the Congress`
    AND `it is the beginning of the first session of the Congress`
    AND `the person has applied in writing`
    AND `the person has certified in the application that the volume is intended for personal use exclusively`
    AND `the volume is the Code of Laws of the United States, the Code of Laws relating to the District of Columbia, or the latest supplement to either`
    AND `the number of copies of that volume the person has already received under section 212 during the term of service` LESS THAN 1

§§ `Section 213 - Appropriation for preparing and editing supplements`

-- src:281 | For preparation and editing an annual appropriation of $6,500 is authorized to carry out the purposes of sections 202 and 203 of this title.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 213 (src:281)
GIVEN `the purpose is the preparation and editing of the supplements of sections 202 and 203` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the annual appropriation in dollars that section 213 authorizes` `the purpose is the preparation and editing of the supplements of sections 202 and 203` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is the preparation and editing of the supplements of sections 202 and 203`
    THEN 6500
    ELSE `section 213 authorizes an appropriation only to carry out the purposes of sections 202 and 203`

@ref 1 U.S.C. s 213 (src:281): the sum is authorized for the purposes of sections 202 and 203 only
GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 213 authorizes an appropriation only to carry out the purposes of sections 202 and 203` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 213 authorizes an appropriation only to carry out the purposes of sections 202 and 203"
